WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:27.291 --> 00:00:28.166
Lord Commander

00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:30.000
Lord Commander! Wake up!

00:00:30.208 --> 00:00:32.333
Giannis? What are you doing here?

00:00:32.333 --> 00:00:33.166
I have to tell you something

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.541
What is it? Did Bango fall off the ladder?

00:00:35.541 --> 00:00:38.375
No. They’re going to exile you. At dawn

00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:39.375
[Sighs]

00:00:39.375 --> 00:00:40.791
I knew this day would come

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:43.083
Demand a trial…a trial by one-on-one!

00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:44.583
I will be your champion!

00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:45.916
Giannis, you’re a good kid

00:00:45.916 --> 00:00:48.208
No, you’re a good Kidd!

00:00:48.208 --> 00:00:50.541
It’s not right. They blame you for everything!

00:00:50.541 --> 00:00:51.416
Eh. Well

00:00:51.416 --> 00:00:54.708
The analytics maesters blame you for all the corner
threes we give up!

00:00:54.708 --> 00:00:56.750
I mean, it is my defensive scheme, so

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:01.083
And the fanlings say it’s your fault we don’t know
when to foul in the last two minutes of battle!

00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:03.166
Yeah, well okay, I mean, that one sort of

00:01:03.166 --> 00:01:05.333
Even though half the knights have given up on you!

00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:06.791
Eleven of them, actually

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:07.791
Here

00:01:08.166 --> 00:01:09.583
What is it? Breakfast smoothie?

00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:11.416
Something like that

00:01:11.416 --> 00:01:12.083
[Coughs]

00:01:12.083 --> 00:01:14.000
I think your strawberries went bad

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.041
Listen, Giannis

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.750
I could adjust my schemes

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.375
I could stop blaming our youth

00:01:19.375 --> 00:01:21.416
I could even work on my time management

00:01:21.916 --> 00:01:23.125
But I won't

00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:25.125
Because at the end of the day

00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:27.666
I must be true to who I am

00:01:27.666 --> 00:01:29.416
In here

00:01:29.416 --> 00:01:30.750
And in here

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.125
I am an asshole

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:37.291
I’m a stubborn asshole and I don’t have a clue what I’m doing

00:01:37.291 --> 00:01:40.250
But...but you’re the best Lord Commander I’ve ever had

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.833
I’m the only Lord Commander you’ve ever had

00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:46.333
Wait, did you have Larry Drew for a year? Were you...

00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:47.708
Did you have Larry Drew for a year?

00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:49.333
Yeah, yes, who cares?

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:52.208
What matters is that it’s not fair what they do to you!

00:01:52.208 --> 00:01:52.500
[Glass breaks]

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.666
[Glass breaks]
You’re giving up on us! You’re giving up on me!

00:01:53.666 --> 00:01:55.416
You’re giving up on us! You’re giving up on me!

00:01:56.333 --> 00:01:59.291
Don’t cry over spilled mead, Giannis! 

00:01:59.291 --> 00:01:59.333
Don’t cry over spilled mead, Giannis! 
When life gives you spilled mead...ugh

00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:01.625
When life gives you spilled mead...ugh

00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:04.500
Use it to get a free timeout…

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.041
-Ah, the Big Dog

00:02:17.375 --> 00:02:21.333
Glenn Robinson. One of House Bucks’ finest knights

00:02:21.791 --> 00:02:25.166
I fought beside him under House Hawks. Years ago

00:02:25.208 --> 00:02:26.916
Lord Commander never talked about him

00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:31.708
But sometimes I’d find him down here lighting candles and praying to the statue

00:02:31.708 --> 00:02:32.958
Those weren’t prayers

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.708
They were curses

00:02:35.291 --> 00:02:38.833
Ser Glenn Robinson was the first pick of his draft class

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.958
Do you know who was second?

00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:41.708
Lord Commander?

00:02:41.708 --> 00:02:44.916
Aye. Well, Ex-Lord Commander

00:02:44.916 --> 00:02:47.208
He would come down here to pay his disrespects

00:02:47.541 --> 00:02:51.791
That resentment, that anger, that was Ser Kidd’s greatest weapon

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:53.708
and his greatest weakness

00:02:53.916 --> 00:02:54.916
[Sighs]

00:02:55.291 --> 00:02:57.250
We were just getting comfortable in his scheme

00:02:57.916 --> 00:02:59.750
Ser Ray Allen

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.833
He was pretty comfortable fighting under George Karl

00:03:03.041 --> 00:03:05.833
They spent years on the brink of conquering the East together

00:03:06.125 --> 00:03:07.291
But they never did

00:03:07.583 --> 00:03:09.083
Things grew toxic

00:03:09.416 --> 00:03:12.333
Five years later, Ray was finally a champion

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:14.416
under Maester Rivers

00:03:14.416 --> 00:03:16.416
his sixth Lord Commander

00:03:17.083 --> 00:03:20.750
His Airness, Ser Jordan was a great knight under Doug Collins

00:03:21.166 --> 00:03:24.875
but it was under the Zen Maester that he became a champion

00:03:25.333 --> 00:03:26.750
-Don’t forget about Steph Curry, mate!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:27.583
Ah!
What the? Delly?

00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:29.625
He was quite comfortable with Mark Jackson

00:03:29.625 --> 00:03:31.250
but Steve Kerr really put him over the top

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:32.791
What are you even doing down here?

00:03:32.791 --> 00:03:34.375
I was just down here scrapping around

00:03:34.375 --> 00:03:37.041
Actually found a pretty cool cave. You guys wanna come check this out?

00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:41.500
Wow. What is this place?

00:03:41.833 --> 00:03:44.083
This must be pre-merger

00:03:44.083 --> 00:03:46.833
Ancient House Hawks maybe?

00:03:47.291 --> 00:03:48.458
I don't know

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:51.791
Is that–is that Wilt Chamberlain?

00:03:51.791 --> 00:03:56.333
Nay. George Mikan. The first giant

00:03:56.333 --> 00:03:56.375
Nay. George Mikan. The first giant
What–what is this? Look at all these pale dwarves

00:03:56.375 --> 00:03:59.916
What–what is this? Look at all these pale dwarves

00:03:59.916 --> 00:04:03.666
Oh my gods, these must be the White Men of the Forest

00:04:03.666 --> 00:04:05.958
I only heard about them in stories

00:04:05.958 --> 00:04:07.750
They were first to play this game

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.000
Looks normal to me

00:04:09.625 --> 00:04:12.458
Look here. No three-point line

00:04:12.458 --> 00:04:14.625
Why is he holding the ball like that?

00:04:14.625 --> 00:04:16.583
They were too weak to shoot overhand

00:04:16.583 --> 00:04:19.125
Some of these guys weren’t even full-time knights

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:22.000
They were tooth maesters when they weren’t playing

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:24.250
Man, this thing must be thousands of years old

00:04:24.458 --> 00:04:25.583
Oh look over here

00:04:25.833 --> 00:04:27.333
This guy's holding a basket

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.458
This looks like the earliest drawing

00:04:29.458 --> 00:04:31.750
Oh yeah, that must be Maester Naismith

00:04:32.125 --> 00:04:32.916
Wow

00:04:33.166 --> 00:04:37.000
Legend has it, he settled Balleros and made our holy sport

00:04:37.208 --> 00:04:38.750
He’s the father of us all

00:04:39.458 --> 00:04:41.750
There, yeah! Look! It says here

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:43.333
Thou Maker. That’s him!

00:04:43.333 --> 00:04:45.750
Wait...wait. That’s not a...

00:04:46.583 --> 00:04:49.500
That says Thon! Thon Maker!

00:04:50.333 --> 00:04:51.708
Uh, Jason?

00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:53.958
How old did you say this was again?

